# Questions & Answers

---

## 1. Do you use computers?

### 💡 Ideas

- Yes
- Every day
- Software engineering
- Study and entertainment

### 🗣️ Sample Answer

Yes, absolutely. As a software engineer, I use a computer every single day for programming, debugging applications, and learning new technologies. Besides work, I also use it for IELTS preparation, watching educational videos, and staying in touch with friends and family.

---

## 2. What do you use a computer to do?

### 💡 Ideas

- Coding
- Learning
- Research
- Movies
- Email

### 🗣️ Sample Answer

I use my computer for a wide variety of tasks. Most of the time, I write code, conduct online research, and read technical documentation. I also use it to attend online meetings, watch tutorials, manage my emails, and occasionally relax by watching films or documentaries.

---

## 3. Did you use computers when you were little?

### 💡 Ideas

- Yes
- Basic games
- School work
- Less frequently

### 🗣️ Sample Answer

Yes, but not nearly as much as I do now. When I was younger, I mainly used a computer for playing games, browsing the internet, and completing school assignments. Back then, computers were more of a source of entertainment than a tool for learning or work.

---

## 4. Do people often use computers these days?

### 💡 Ideas

- Yes
- Education
- Business
- Communication

### 🗣️ Sample Answer

Definitely. Computers have become an essential part of modern life. People rely on them for education, work, communication, online shopping, and even healthcare. Although smartphones are becoming increasingly powerful, computers are still indispensable for many professional and academic tasks.

---

## 5. Will people continue to use computers in the future?

### 💡 Ideas

- Yes
- AI
- Remote work
- Technology

### 🗣️ Sample Answer

Without a doubt. As technology continues to advance, computers will become even more powerful and intelligent. Fields such as artificial intelligence, data science, and software development heavily depend on computers, so I believe they will remain an indispensable part of our daily lives for many years to come.

